<title>SINGAPORE: Meiban 1996 net profit up 22.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Meiban 1996 net profit up 22.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to December 31 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			3.37	 vs     2.74</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	     4.35	 vs     3.83</p>
<p>    Dividend (cts)		  1.20	 vs     1.20</p>
<p>    Turnover			 35.47	 vs    27.95</p>
<p>    Other income incl interest  0.23	 vs     0.25</p>
<p>    Depreciation,amortisation   1.58	 vs     0.91</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		  4.31	 vs     3.46</p>
<p>    Associates			0.32	 vs     0.28</p>
<p>    Tax				 1.26	 vs     1.00</p>
<p>Note - Meiban Plastics Ltd said on Thursday its relocation to a new building, coupled with continued weakness in electronics industry, would affect its operations in 1997. However, the group expects 1997 to remain profitable.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
